---
source: tests/snapshots.rs
description: grav --help
expression: run(args)
---
exit: 0
--- stdout
A state-of-the-art file system analyzer with TUI

Usage: grav [OPTIONS] [PATH]
       grav <COMMAND>

Commands:
  scan         Show what takes up space, largest first
  duplicates   Find files with identical contents
  age          Break files down by age and find stale directories
  diff         Show what grew, shrank, appeared or went between two scans
  history      Show how a directory's size changed across recorded scans
  export       Write a complete scan as a JSON snapshot
  init         Print shell integration that follows the explorer's directory on exit
  completions  Print shell completions
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [PATH]  Directory to open in the explorer, or a snapshot to browse [default: current directory]

Options:
  -s, --scan             Start a full scan as soon as the explorer opens
  -A, --apparent-size    Show file lengths instead of disk usage (toggle with `b`)
      --cwd-file <FILE>  Write the explorer's directory at exit to FILE (see `grav init`)
      --print-cwd        Print the explorer's directory at exit
  -h, --help             Print help
  -V, --version          Print version

Global options:
      --color <WHEN>     When to use colour [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
      --binary           Show sizes in powers of 1024 (KiB, MiB) instead of 1000 (kB, MB)
      --log-file <FILE>  Append diagnostic logs to FILE (filter with RUST_LOG) [env:
                         GRAVITYFILE_LOG_FILE]

Run `grav` with no command to open the explorer.

Exit status: 0 success, 1 error, 2 usage error, 3 incomplete results with
--strict, 130 interrupted.
--- stderr
